From 7f38171c399721a81be79423f2b3b46dc973c826 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Victor Ocsa Mamani <aocsa.cs@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 18:20:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(starrocks-fe): plan FILES() scans with real row
 counts instead of 1

The FE planned every FILES() scan at 1 row: 22/22 TPC-H plans had
card_all_one=True and all 126 exchanges were costed from column widths,
so join sides, BROADCAST/SHUFFLE and CTE decisions were data-blind (one
CN broadcast 3.79e9 lineitem rows into q04's semi join). StatisticsCalculator
now asks TableFunctionTable for the count: the parquet footer total when the
compute node reports one (next commit), else total file bytes divided by the
typed row width of the inferred schema, the same rule HiveStatisticsProvider
uses without statistics. Column statistics stay unknown. The mutable FE config
files_scan_estimate_row_count (default true) restores the 1-row plans for an
EXPLAIN COSTS A/B on one running FE.

Ships as patches/files-scan-row-count.patch on the StarRocks submodule
(pointer unchanged); the bench scripts set and read back cbo_cte_reuse=false
on a patched FE, since real costs let the CBO keep a CTE materialised and
the CN refuses MULTI_CAST_DATA_STREAM_SINK.

Tested: FE JUnit TableFunctionTableTest, StatisticsCalculatorTest and the new
FilesScanStatisticsTest (fake:// 3072 B / 20 B = 153 rows; injected 1e9 vs 10
rows gives INNER JOIN (BROADCAST) with the small side building, and the FE
commutes LEFT SEMI to RIGHT SEMI); patch set applies from a clean submodule in
glob order and is idempotent; fe-build 269 s.

Left: the CN translator has no RIGHT_SEMI_JOIN arm, needed before the knob is
on in any sweep; this does not make q05 q08 q09 q17 q18 q21 pass on 1 CN.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
